# apps/ai-service environment variables
#
# Copy this file to apps/ai-service/.env.local (or export the variables in
# your deployment environment) and replace placeholders with real values.
# .env.local is gitignored - real values must NEVER be committed.
#
# Both variables are SERVER-ONLY and are used exclusively by this service.
# Neither may appear in apps/web, in any NEXT_PUBLIC_* variable, or in any
# browser-reachable code.

# --- OPENAI_API_KEY ---
# Why:         Credential for the OpenAI provider (the only holder is this
#              service; apps/web never sees it).
# Provider:    OpenAI -> API keys (https://platform.openai.com/api-keys)
# Scope:       Server-only, secret. Never expose to the browser.
# Placement:   apps/ai-service/.env.local (or deployment env)
# Gitignored:  Yes (.env.local matches .env.* in the root .gitignore).
OPENAI_API_KEY="YOUR_OPENAI_API_KEY_HERE"

# --- AI_SERVICE_SHARED_SECRET ---
# Why:         Service-to-service authentication for POST /generate-mcq and
#              POST /generate-coding (sent by apps/web as the
#              X-AI-Service-Secret header). GET /health requires no secret.
# Provider:    Generate any long random value (e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`).
# Scope:       Server-only, secret. Shared between this service and apps/web
#              (Phase 3C will add AI_SERVICE_URL on the web side).
# Placement:   apps/ai-service/.env.local (and later apps/web/.env.local)
# Gitignored:  Yes.
AI_SERVICE_SHARED_SECRET="YOUR_AI_SERVICE_SHARED_SECRET_HERE"
